    "narrative": "For the August 3rd slate, the Austin Waves look to exploit favorable pitching matchups, with **Jackson Merrill** leading the charge at a 75.26 efficiency score. **Jackson Merrill** represents our highest-upside play today against Pfaadt; the projection model highlights a +13% platoon edge and, crucially, a +2% boost due to Pfaadt\u2019s slow delivery, which provides a high-probability environment for **Jackson Merrill** to secure a stolen base, our most scarce category. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is another essential start, carrying a 73.66 rating. Batting out of the #3 hole against McGreevy, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a combined +27% boost from a strong platoon split and favorable starter skill metrics, positioning him as the offensive anchor of our middle infield.\n\nThe decision to start **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (70.86) remains solid despite a marginal negative platoon adjustment, as his massive ceiling against the struggling Javier (xERA 5.27) keeps his floor comfortably in the elite tier. Conversely, while **Nasim Nunez** (53.07) technically qualifies as a marginal start, he remains the most volatile component of today\u2019s lineup. We opted to maintain **Nasim Nunez** over potential alternatives because his speed profile is necessary to combat our league-wide deficit in stolen bases. **Andy Pages** (60.69) rounds out the roster; while he faces an \"Elite Hold\" pitcher in Boyd, his #2 spot in the order provides enough volume to overcome a slight penalty to his efficiency score.\n\nRegarding the bench, the lack of depth for today\u2019s lineup is largely driven by external circumstances. With **Gunnar Henderson**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Jorge Polanco** sidelined due to team off-days, our bench optimization was restricted. **Jordan Westburg** remains our most significant inactive asset as he continues his recovery on the IL. While we are currently carrying prospects like **Jacob Wilson**, **Cole Carrigg**, and **Luis Lara** on the deeper bench, none have the current ATC projection parity to displace our active starters in a high-leverage Roto environment. We are monitoring weather reports for the **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages** game closely, as any wind shifts in this venue could negatively impact their fly-ball-heavy profiles against the lefty Boyd.",
